{"name":"Imagery","hex":"#7a6e70","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"imagery","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The work of one who makes images or visible representation of objects.","Imitation work."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imagery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Imagery","blocks":[{"text":"Imagery is the literary device of using sensory language: figurative language that evokes a mental image or other kinds of vivid sense impressions in the reader's or listener's imagination. Less commonly known by the Greek term enargia, imagery can also be instrumental, in storytelling, for conveying tone, mood, symbolism, and other narrative elements."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imagery","wikidata":"Q4817665"},{"title":"Imagery (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Imagery is the debut studio album by Canadian death metal band Neuraxis. It was released in 1997, through the band's own record label, Neoblast Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/Neuraxis_-_Imagery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imagery_(album)","wikidata":"Q6002322"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"imagery":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/En-us-imagery.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/21/En-us-imagery.ogg/En-us-imagery.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey rectangle","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Grey_rectangle.jpg/500px-Grey_rectangle.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_rectangle.jpg","share":0.664375},{"title":"Hurricane Agnes Satellite imagery, June 17, 1972","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Hurricane_Agnes_Satellite_imagery%2C_June_17%2C_1972.jpg/500px